We open-sourced a method to cut slop from agent-generated code. It seriously works, and we have receipts — PRs on production code merge 2.4 times faster while still maintaining quality.

See Xingyao's post below for details on *The Verification Stack*.

@xingyaow: "Coding agents open PRs in minutes. But on consequential codebases, those PRs still wait days for human review. So we built a verification stack, and on our own repo, it cut time-to-merge by 58% without lowering code quality. Here’s how."
